export anchor CRTScanlinesStyle:
    number: 291
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: CRT scanlines
    idea: The review is broadcast like a teletext page on a curved colour CRT, set in a rounded plastic bezel with scanlines, a soft vignette and a hint of red and cyan fringing, its sections marked by solid colour bands and block mosaic graphics.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bezel: #2b2925, the plastic frame around the screen
        bezelEdge: #4a463f, the bezel highlight and the power lamp ring
        tube: #020713, the screen and the style sheet background
        panel: #0a1630, boxed areas inside the screen, the diff and the style sheet cards
        white: #f2f6ff, main text
        cyan: #4ff2ff, the page header, links, the cyan band and focus
        yellow: #ffe94d, the title, requested changes and the yellow band
        magenta: #ff7cf5, labels, line numbers and the magenta band
        green: #5cff8f, passed, approved, Open and added lines
        red: #ff6a6a, failing and removed lines
        blueBand: #1e3cff, the blue band behind white text
        bandInk: #020713, text on the cyan, yellow, green and magenta bands
        scanline: #000000, the 1px dark line every 3px across the screen, drawn at 20 percent opacity
    type:
        A chunky monospace stack, Bedstead, MODE7, Courier New, DejaVu Sans Mono,
        ui-monospace, set bold everywhere so the strokes stay crisp through the
        scanlines. Base 16px on 1.5. The title is double height at 30px. Band labels
        16px caps tracked 0.12em. The page header 14px. Headings carry a 1px red and
        cyan fringe.
    layout:
        The page sits inside a CRT. A dark plastic bezel with 28px padding and a
        power lamp frames a tube with 36px by 56px rounded corners, an inset
        vignette and a scanline overlay. Inside, a teletext layout. A cyan header
        line reads P214, Brightwork Code and the date and time. A block mosaic B
        logo sits beside the owner and repository, Private, and Watch 12, Star 48
        and Fork 3. The six tabs follow as page numbers 100 to 600 with Pull
        requests on a yellow band. Then the double height yellow title with number
        214, the Open marker and the merge sentence. Below, two columns. The left
        has a green CHECKS band with a twelve block mosaic meter and the failing
        check named, then a magenta FILES band with the three files, then a blue
        DIFF band and the boxed hunk with the comment. The right has a yellow
        REVIEWS band, a cyan DETAILS band with assignees, labels, milestone and
        linked issue, and the disabled merge button with its reason. Below 900px the
        columns stack and the bezel thins to 10px.
    spacing: A character grid. 8px band padding, 16px between bands, 32px inside the tube.
    density: Medium. Big chunky text in short rows, like a broadcast page.
    corners: The bezel is 40px round and the tube 36px by 56px. Everything inside is square.
    borders:
        No rules inside the screen. Solid colour bands mark sections. The diff and
        comment sit in panel boxes with a 2px cyan edge.
    shadows:
        A large inset vignette on the tube, a soft outer shadow under the bezel, and
        a faint cyan glow around the tube. Headings carry 1px red and cyan offset
        text shadows.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2.5px stroke at 1em, bold enough to read through scanlines,
        always with the word. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square
        for failing, triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the
        blocked merge.
    focus: A 3px cyan outline offset 2px with a 6px dark gap.
    tone:
        Broadcast caption voice in caps for bands, plain sentences for content, such
        as CHECKS and 11 of 12 checks passed.
